cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "litsurvey: multi-source scientific literature search with LLM-assisted novelty assessment"
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Khankhoje
    given-names: Uday
    email: uday@ee.iitm.ac.in
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Electrical Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology
      Madras
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9629-3922'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/udaykdk/litsurvey'
abstract: >-
  A zero-dependency Python tool for literature surveys: it searches OpenAlex,
  Semantic Scholar, arXiv, TechRxiv, Research Square and the IACR ePrint
  archive, fuses and de-duplicates the results, walks the citation graph,
  finds open-access copies, and exports BibTeX/RIS/CSV. An LLM (a local
  model, the user's Claude Code / Codex / Gemini subscription CLI, or a cloud
  API) drives multi-step novelty assessment and cited state-of-the-art
  surveys, with a reproducible search log. A local browser interface with
  run history is included. Designed so that confidential manuscript content
  never has to leave the user's machine.
keywords:
  - literature search
  - peer review
  - systematic review
  - novelty assessment
  - Semantic Scholar
  - OpenAlex
  - arXiv
  - BibTeX
  - large language models
